Z||000000||conductor||11-17-2001||10:23 AM||||Ok, does the 4cyl have a ticking noise (like TRRRRRRRRRR)coming out of the aircleaner housing? <BR>I can hear it very good when I lay my ear on it.<BR>Is this usual?<BR>Ecm says code 35.<BR>Also should the connectors be very clean from the inside, or is there always some dirt in it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||maryjane||11-17-2001||10:56 AM||||not sure about the noise. You could be hearing the injector, the pvc valve, or blowby. Code 35 is idle air control., but anything affecting your idle may produce this code. If the inside of the tbi is dirty, check your air cleaner assy for openings or leaks. I think there is also a little foam filter for the valve cover vent on the left side of the cover. Should be under the air cleaner horn. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-17-2001||06:45 PM||||It may be your IAC valve or a dirty/ old injector.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mattyman||11-17-2001||08:42 PM||||I always hear a very faint buzzing/humming noise in my 87 coupe.  Im not really sure what it is.  Seems as though its coming from the rear drivers side.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||11-17-2001||10:08 PM||||I'm pretty sure you're hearing the injector.  It's normal for it to be rather noisy.  The first time I took the air cleaner cover off my 84 and started the engine I was surprised at how much noise it makes!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
